# RED run — on-disk deletion of ONE version surface, gate red — 2026-07-31

Demonstrates the four-surface predicate is not vacuous at the artifact level: with three
surfaces left byte-intact, deleting only the AfterInstall output line in the BUILT
`site/dist/download/index.html` turns the gate red. (The four individual deletion
controls live inside the gate itself — see the green run and the test file.)

## mutate the built /download (only the AfterInstall output line)

    perl -0pi -e 's#<span class="ui-code__line">cswarm 0\.1\.4 \(protocol 0\.1\.0\)</span>#<span class="ui-code__line"></span>#' site/dist/download/index.html

    afterinstall output count -> 0   (removed)
    footer line count         -> 1   (still present)
    visible pin + copy payload      (still present — untouched)

## same gate, standalone, against the mutated artifact

    node --import tsx --test site/scripts/download-version.test.mjs
    exit=1
    ℹ tests 6
    ℹ pass  0
    ℹ fail  6

Every green-path assertion now fails because the page is missing one of the four surfaces.

## restore, proven byte-identical while both files exist

    cp /tmp/dl-backup.html site/dist/download/index.html
    cmp site/dist/download/index.html /tmp/dl-backup.html   -> identical (cmp exits 0)
    sha256sum site/dist/download/index.html                 -> 17998fb01cd8af66104a47a3527e361b791945a787dca8521e58774a923a5aa7

## gate rerun against the restored artifact

    ℹ tests 6
    ℹ pass  6
    ℹ fail  0
